Prompt: adapt_screenplay.j2
Service Step: ADAPT_SCREENPLAY (finished-text backflow level 2: semantic adaptation)
Purpose: Rewrite the scenes/dialogue/action produced by the level-1
         deterministic projection into shootable film scenes: narration becomes
         visual action, psychology is externalized, dialogue is trimmed for
         shot rhythm. Outputs a complete Screenplay object (FULL_OBJECT); each
         scene is accepted only after passing semantic validation.
Upstream Input:
  - title/language: work title and output language
  - scenes: level-1 projected scenes (lines/source_refs are the only canon source)
  - direction: directional metadata (emotion arc / pace / intent summaries,
    progressive disclosure, never the full text)
  - cast_names: registered cast list (the rewrite must not invent characters)
Downstream Output:
  - JSON (FULL_OBJECT): {"title":..., "synopsis":..., "scenes":[<ScreenplayScene>]}
  - Downstream consumers:
    * film/pipeline SCREENPLAY stage: per-scene accept/reject before adoption
    * Storyboard stage: consumes objective/conflict/visual_hook of adapted scenes
Consumption-chain priority:
  P0 = fidelity: never add/remove characters, never change outcomes or causality;
       keep source_refs verbatim
  P1 = visualization: narration/psychology must become visible action, gesture,
       props or spatial change
  P2 = rhythm: trim dialogue into short shot-paced lines, drop literary clauses
Brief example:
  Input: scenes=[{"heading":"Rainy farewell","lines":[{"kind":"action","text":"He knew this was their last meeting."}]}]
  Output: scenes=[{"heading":"Rainy farewell","lines":[{"kind":"action","text":"He reaches for the door handle, then stops mid-air."},{"kind":"dialogue","speaker":"Lin Yuan","text":"Don't see me off."}]}]
